# Curious Obsession: "At the beginning of your end step, if you didn't attack with a creature this turn, sacrifice this Aura."
# Bot1's Savannah Lions attacks on turn 3 BEFORE the Aura exists (the ruling: any creature that attacked counts, not only
# the enchanted one, and the Aura asks the whole turn's history), so the Aura cast in the second main phase stays through
# turn 3's end step. On turn 5 nothing attacks - turn 3's attack does not count - and the Aura is sacrificed (CR 603.4, 508.1).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Savannah Lions
Curious Obsession
Plains x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Savannah Lions.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Savannah Lions > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Curious Obsession.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Savannah Lions)
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Curious Obsession.AttachedTo = Savannah Lions
[T5 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Curious Obsession = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard = Curious Obsession
